---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const experience = [
  {
    role: 'Senior DevOps Engineer · Cloud Platform',
    company: 'Cardo AI',
    period: 'February 2026 - Present',
    paragraphs: [
      'Joining Cardo AI marked an exciting new chapter for me. Moving into fintech meant learning how to build and operate platforms where reliability, security, and trust are part of every decision. I work across a multi-region AWS environment and its Kubernetes platforms, helping provide the foundation for a cloud-native product used by institutional clients in Europe and the US.',
      'A large part of my work is about making the platform easier to use and safer to change. I have built automation around Terraform, GitOps, GitHub Actions, and AWS CodeBuild, while also improving how security and compliance are embedded in everyday engineering rather than treated as separate activities. I have worked on policy as code, SOC2 readiness, and FinOps initiatives, and I continue to explore practical uses of n8n and AI to remove repetitive work and leave more room for thoughtful engineering.',
    ],
  },
  {
    role: 'DevOps Engineer · Team Lead',
    company: 'Florence Consulting Group',
    period: 'December 2019 - January 2026',
    paragraphs: [
      'Florence Consulting Group was my first real job, and I will always be grateful to its CEOs, Iacopo and Niccolò, for giving me the opportunity to grow there. I joined as a Junior and gradually found my way into DevOps, taking on increasingly complex technical and organizational responsibilities until I became Team Lead. That journey shaped how I approach engineering: stay curious, take ownership, and make difficult systems understandable for the people who operate them.',
      'Consulting gave me the chance to work across cloud, hybrid, and on-premises environments, helping teams move from legacy systems toward more maintainable cloud-native platforms. I designed infrastructure with code, introduced Kubernetes and GitOps practices, improved delivery pipelines, and built observability around the systems we supported. As my role grew, I also mentored engineers and worked with senior stakeholders on strategy, partnerships, and how technical work could create lasting value for the business. Much of the day-to-day improvement came from small tools and automations in Python and Bash that removed friction from recurring operational work.',
    ],
  },
  {
    role: 'Junior Programmer (School/Work Alternation)',
    company: 'OSItalia',
    period: 'June 2018 - September 2018',
    paragraphs: [
      'My time at OSItalia was my first opportunity to see what software development looked like in a professional environment. I learned the fundamentals of programming patterns and object-oriented design with Delphi, then applied them while building a database management application. More than any specific technology, the experience taught me how much care, communication, and patience go into turning an idea into something people can actually use.',
    ],
  },
];

const skills = [
  { group: 'Cloud', items: ['AWS', 'Azure', 'GCP'] },
  { group: 'Containers & Orchestration', items: ['Kubernetes (EKS)', 'KEDA', 'Karpenter'] },
  { group: 'Infrastructure as Code', items: ['Terraform'] },
  { group: 'CI/CD', items: ['GitHub Actions', 'GitLab CI/CD', 'Jenkins', 'Azure DevOps'] },
  { group: 'GitOps & Platform Engineering', items: ['ArgoCD', 'Helm', 'Kustomize'] },
  { group: 'DevOps Practices', items: ['DevSecOps', 'Automation', 'FinOps'] },
  { group: 'Security', items: ['Container Security', 'Cloud Security', 'Kubernetes Security', 'Prowler', 'Trivy'] },
  { group: 'Observability', items: ['Grafana (LGTM)', 'Elastic Stack'] },
  { group: 'Programming & Scripting', items: ['Python', 'Bash'] },
];

const certifications = [
  { name: 'AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Associate', active: true },
  { name: 'GitLab Solutions Architect Core Verified Associate', active: true },
  { name: 'CKS: Certified Kubernetes Security Specialist', active: false },
  { name: 'CKA: Certified Kubernetes Administrator', active: false },
  { name: 'CKAD: Certified Kubernetes Application Developer', active: false },
  { name: 'KCNA: Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate', active: false },
  { name: 'KCSA: Kubernetes and Cloud Native Security Associate', active: false },
];
---

<Base
  title="Alessandro Quadrini - Senior DevOps Engineer"
  description="Portfolio of Alessandro Quadrini, Senior DevOps and Platform Engineer with 7+ years of experience building secure, scalable cloud-native platforms."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <img src="/me.jpg" alt="Portrait of Alessandro Quadrini" class="avatar" width="400" height="400" />
    <div>
      <p class="hero-hello">Hello! I'm</p>
      <h1>Alessandro Quadrini</h1>
      <p class="hero-role">Senior DevOps &amp; Platform Engineer</p>
      <p class="hero-tagline">
        I design and run cloud-native platforms that are secure, scalable, and cost-effective;
        and I have a lot of fun doing it.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-links">
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:quadrini.alessandro@proton.me">Email me</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alessandro-quadrini" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://github.com/alequadro" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://alequadro.github.io/resume" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resume</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="container">
    <h2>About me</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a Senior DevOps and Platform Engineer with 7+ years of experience designing and
      operating cloud-native platforms across many sectors. I've led DevOps teams, driven cloud
      transformation programs, and delivered secure, scalable infrastructure for enterprise and
      regulated environments.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm always looking for stimulating challenges that keep expanding my knowledge. If you
      have one, I'd love to hear about it!
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="experience" class="container">
    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      {
        experience.map((job) => (
          <article class="card job">
            <header>
              <h3>{job.role}</h3>
              <p class="job-meta">
                <span class="job-company">{job.company}</span> &middot; {job.period}
              </p>
            </header>
            <div class="job-narrative">
              {job.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
            </div>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="life" class="container">
    <h2>Beyond Work</h2>
      <p>I developed a passion for computers at around the age of six, when my father brought home a custom-built PC. I still vividly remember the transition from floppy disks to CDs. At the time, I barely understood their purpose, but I was fascinated by every new piece of technology.</p>
      <p>Gaming has always been a big part of my life and remains one of my greatest passions. Looking back, it's what sparked my interest in computers, hardware, and software, eventually leading me toward a career in IT.</p> 
      <p>Outside of work (which I believe is important to balance with personal interests!) I enjoy working out and listening to music. And yes, I'm a huge Michael Jackson fan!</p>
      <p>You might also be wondering why I chose "alequadro" as my name. It is simply a combination of my two nicknames: Ale and Quadro.
        Ale is pretty self-explanatory, while Quadro is a nickname my friends gave me when I moved to Tuscany in 2009. Somehow, it stuck with me ever since and has become a part of my identity.</p>
    </section>

  <section id="skills" class="container">
    <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
    <div class="skills-grid">
      {
        skills.map((skill) => (
          <div class="card skill-group">
            <h3>{skill.group}</h3>
            <ul class="tags">
              {skill.items.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="certifications" class="container">
    <h2>Certifications</h2>
    <ul class="cert-list">
      {
        certifications.map((cert) => (
          <li class="card cert">
            <span>{cert.name}</span>
            {!cert.active && <span class="badge">expired</span>}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="cert-note">
      Former Kubestronaut; the Kubernetes certifications above lapsed only because renewal fees
      added up. The knowledge stayed!
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="education" class="container">
    <h2>Education &amp; Languages</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>I.T.I.S. Tullio Buzzi</h3>
      <p>High School Degree in Computer Science and Telecommunications</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Languages</h3>
      <p>Italian (native) &middot; English (fluent, C1)</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 4rem;
  }

  .avatar {
    width: clamp(10rem, 25vw, 14rem);
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 3px solid var(--accent);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .hero-hello {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }

  .hero-role {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .hero-tagline {
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .hero-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-weight: 600;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  .btn:hover {
    text-decoration: none;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px var(--accent-soft);
  }

  .btn-outline {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .card {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .timeline {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .job h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .job-meta {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .job-company {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .job-narrative p {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
  }

  .job-narrative p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .skills-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .skill-group h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .tags li {
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .cert-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .cert {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .badge {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
  }

  .cert-note {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  #education .card {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  #education p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .hero {
      flex-direction: column;
      text-align: center;
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .hero-links {
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .hero-tagline {
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
